# CORE ARCHITECTURE RULES

## SSOT RULE (HARD)
Each domain owns its data + logic.

No duplicate ownership allowed.

Never split a domain across modules.

------------------------------------------------

## PLATFORM RULE
Platform defines HOW execution works.

Business modules define WHAT exists.

Platform NEVER contains domain behavior.

------------------------------------------------

## LOGIC RULE (CRITICAL)

Business logic must exist ONLY once.

Never duplicate:

- lifecycle rules
- state transitions
- ownership rules
- workflow logic
- triggers
- domain functions

------------------------------------------------

## MIGRATION RULE (IMPORTANT CLARIFICATION)

Migration numbers are NOT architecture.

Domains are the SSOT.

A domain evolves over multiple migrations:

Example:
- 003_devices_rev19.sql
- 024_devices_extensions_rev19.sql
- 041_devices_automation_rev20.sql

All belong to the SAME domain.

❗ You must NEVER move logic to another module just because a migration is newer.

If new functionality is needed:
→ Add a new migration in the SAME domain

NOT:
→ Edge
→ Another module

------------------------------------------------

## EDGE LAYER (API ONLY)

Edge is strictly a transport layer.

Allowed in Edge:

- RPC wrappers
- auth guards
- authorization checks
- tenant validation
- request validation
- response formatting
- logging helpers
- API utilities

❗ Edge must NEVER contain:

- business logic
- workflows
- state transitions
- device logic
- booking logic
- CRM logic
- commerce logic
- logistics logic

RULE:
Edge only CALLS domain functions.

Never owns behavior.

------------------------------------------------

## DECISION RULE (WHEN UNCLEAR)

If ownership is unclear:

STOP

Identify the single SSOT module.

If two modules seem responsible → architecture is wrong.

Never create dual ownership.

------------------------------------------------